# Read the current TCP pose (robot base frame, mm / deg) straight from the
# controller, expressed in `tool_number` (-1 = the ACTIVE tool, see
# /cobot/set_active_tool). /cobot/state carries the same pose at the poll
# rate; use this service only when you need a specific non-active tool or a
# pose+joints pair read back-to-back (teach / remember flows).
int32 tool_number -1
---
bool success
float64 x
float64 y
float64 z
float64 rx
float64 ry
float64 rz
int32 tool_number         # tool file the pose above is expressed in
float64[] joints_deg      # S L U R B T at the same instant (empty if the joint read failed)
int32 status_code
string message
